quantile_over_time(0.5, up[3m]): the median of the samples in the window
[('instance','host1')]	20
[('instance','host2')]	15
[('instance','host3')]	100
quantile_over_time(0, up[3m]) and quantile_over_time(1, up[3m]): the minimum and the maximum
[('instance','host1')]	10
[('instance','host2')]	5
[('instance','host3')]	100
[('instance','host1')]	30
[('instance','host2')]	25
[('instance','host3')]	100
quantile_over_time(0.25, up[3m]): interpolated between the two lower samples
[('instance','host1')]	15
[('instance','host2')]	10
[('instance','host3')]	100
a level outside [0, 1] gives -Inf or +Inf and a NaN level gives NaN, like in Prometheus
[('instance','host1')]	inf
[('instance','host2')]	inf
[('instance','host3')]	inf
[('instance','host1')]	-inf
[('instance','host2')]	-inf
[('instance','host3')]	-inf
[('instance','host1')]	nan
[('instance','host2')]	nan
[('instance','host3')]	nan
the level may be a scalar expression that is only known when the query runs
[('instance','host1')]	20
[('instance','host2')]	15
[('instance','host3')]	100
the level may vary with the evaluation time: one level per step of a range query
[('instance','host1')]	[(1700000000,10),(1700000001,30)]
[('instance','host2')]	[(1700000000,5),(1700000001,25)]
[('instance','host3')]	[(1700000000,100),(1700000001,100)]
quantile_over_time with a fixed @, range query: the same quantile at every step
[('instance','host1')]	[20,20,20,20]
[('instance','host2')]	[15,15,15,15]
[('instance','host3')]	[100,100,100,100]
